+/*
+ * Measured: the short window, written in a register group, lands on the next
+ * frame with 0x3802 = 0 and a frame later with 0x3802 = 1; the other
+ * registers land on the next frame. A window that shrinks by more than the
+ * frame's spare rows costs one short frame, unless it lands a frame late and
+ * the frame before it is longer by the difference. That is the OEM Windows
+ * driver's sequence; sc200pc_unstretch() takes the extra rows back.
+ */
